.TH ALX-LINK 1 "November 2026" "Algothix OS 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
alx-link \- lightweight cross-device workspace layer for Algothix OS (ALX) Lite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alx-link pair
\fB\-\-listen\fR [\fB\-\-code\fR \fIPIN\fR]
.br
.B alx-link pair
\fIpeer\fR \fB\-\-code\fR \fIPIN\fR
.br
.B alx-link send
\fIfile\fR [\fIpeer\fR]
.br
.B alx-link clip
[\fIpeer\fR]
.br
.B alx-link notify
\fIpeer\fR \fImessage...\fR
.br
.B alx-link run
\fIpeer\fR \fB\-\-\fR \fIcommand...\fR
.br
.B alx-link status
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B alx-link unpair
\fIpeer\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B alx-link
pairs Algothix OS machines over Tailscale (default) or WireGuard using an
HMAC-SHA256 6-digit PIN handshake, exchanging ed25519 SSH keys and configuring
Syncthing (\fI~/ALX-Sync\fR at \fBNice=10\fR / \fBIOSchedulingClass=idle\fR,
enabled only after pairing). File transfers use Taildrop (\fBtailscale file cp\fR)
on Tailscale or \fBrsync\fR/\fBscp\fR over SSH on WireGuard. Clipboard push
(\fBclip\fR) and notifications (\fBnotify\fR) run over SSH with remote X11 and
D-Bus environment resolution.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/alx/link.conf
.br
.I ~/.config/alx-link/peers/*.json
.br
.I ~/.ssh/config.d/alx-link-*.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR syncthing (1),
.BR notify-send (1)
